hi guys it's me quinn and as always if  you appreciate my content consider  hitting the like button it's the only  way the youtube algorithm really notices  me so of course i've made a lot of dune  content on this channel but recently  i've been doing shorter videos for  people that might have seen the doom  movie but have not read the books just  to give those people some information  about what is going on we've talked  about why there's no robots in the  series we've talked about the politics  of dune we've talked about the emperor  and the beanie jesuit sisterhood now  it's time to get into what exactly paul  atreides saw in his visions that freaked  him out so badly now the book refers to  this as the terrible purpose and paul  actually begins to sense this very early  on in the novel paul atreides was bred  by the benny jesuit sisterhood as a tool  of control they have spent centuries  doing the groundwork and preparing the  universe for the coming of their quizets  hadorak and on arrakis their myths and  legends very easily took root because  the fremen were descended from the zin  sunni wanderers who before they got to  arrakis had been oppressed chased from  planet to planet never finding a true  home a culture born from this type of  society the bini jesuit knew were extra  susceptible to legends about a savior  messiah figure who would free them from  oppression so after being shifted from  planet to planet facing oppression on  every planet and after being oppressed  by the empire and the harkonnens  brutally for the past  nearly a century here comes paul  atreides who seems to fit the myths and  legends exactly when people truly  believe that a person is god whatever  that person says becomes the will of god  and because  god is realized in an actual form  the proof of his existence constantly  reinforces itself this is fertile ground  for fanaticism and that's exactly what  paul is seeing in his visions paul wants  to gain vengeance for house atreides but  in doing so  he kinda has to let the fremen believe  he is a god and when the fremen fight  for him they're not just fighting for  another leader they're fighting for a  messiah any war that the freeman might  fight in the name of paul atreides is a  holy war in allowing the freeman to  believe he is god paul will release a  fanatic religion onto the universe a  religion that will seek to convert all  non-believers they will be armed with  the certainty that their god paul  atreides is the one true god the one  true messiah and all those who  disbelieve cannot join in the kingdom of  heaven and once a fanatic religion like  this is unleashed it cannot be undone it  cannot be controlled it has momentum of  its own which goes beyond the mortal man  paul the trees paul is seeing a war rage  on and on in his name endless death in  his name unstoppable and totally outside  of his control a curious thing that the  movie does is that you can see when paul  is seeing these visions in the movie  that they disturb him incredibly and  even blames the benny jesuit sisterhood  and his mother for doing this to him and  yet at this point in time these visions  are not set in stone paul sees possible  futures it's important to note however  that at the end of the movie jessica  wants paul off of the world paul  actively makes the choice to stay on  arrakis full well knowing that the path  for atreides vengeance leads to an  unstoppable holy war he actively makes  that decision the fact that this is  shown explicitly in the movie shows us  that paul is kind of a great character  he's not the typical disney protagonist  that's perfect in most ways he's highly  skilled highly trained and yet fallible  and certainly not a messiah as many of  the freemen already believe frank  herbert writer of the original dune  series famously stated that he wrote the  dune series as a warning against  charismatic leaders he firmly believed  that when people threw their faith  behind a leader blindly it led to  catastrophe and that is essentially what  is being depicted in the dune series i  hope that helps explain it for you guys  thanks so much for watching make sure  you like and subscribe for more science  fiction lore just check out my channel  to find out all the series i cover  organized neatly into playlist
 

